  "findings": [
    "After a converter parent exited, inherited stdout/stderr handles kept the output tasks pending. Caller cancellation and the five-second process deadline both failed to settle during an eight-second test observation window.",
    "The previous owner awaited process exit before observing reader failure and did not pass cancellation to reads."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Supervise exit and both output tasks together, observing any failure immediately.",
    "Pass the shared caller/deadline token into every read and check before/after, including EOF.",
    "On failure cancel sibling reads, request active-process-tree termination and await all observations before preserving the original outcome.",
    "Preserve an observed converter-output-limit failure over concurrent cancellation; remove the redundant private overflow exception.",
    "Clarify active-tree termination versus OS containment across package/companion documentation."
  ],
